<http://data.silknow.org/object/9aaa3d50-e32d-3150-a955-9397a566d331>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "At the end of the 18th century embroidery designs began to develop into rigid and heavily stylised borders for towels and napkins. The colours of 18th and 19th century embroideries were originally very bright but many have faded to pleasing pastel shades; often great quantities of metal thread were used. Napkins were mainly used to clean fingers during meals, but were also used as decoration and as covers. Their designs were consistently inventive."@en , "Border, cotton embroidered with silk in double running in steps and double running variations. There is one motif, repeated side-by-side: it is a diagonal stem with three pink flowers, each with six petals, four smaller blue flowers, three white leaves and some small yellow leaves.\nThere is evidence that a second width was originally attached along the selvedge.\nOne sidehas been cut and hemmed."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/992efba2-d720-3360-a40d-68aaa1119f72> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "At the end of the 18th century embroidery designs began to develop into rigid and heavily stylised borders for towels and napkins. The colours of 18th and 19th century embroideries were originally very bright but many have faded to pleasing pastel shades; often great quantities of metal thread were used. Napkins were mainly used to clean fingers during meals, but were also used as decoration and as covers. Their designs were consistently inventive."@en , "Border, cotton embroidered with silk in double running in steps and double running variations. There is one motif, repeated side-by-side: it is a diagonal stem with three pink flowers, each with six petals, four smaller blue flowers, three white leaves and some small yellow leaves.\nThere is evidence that a second width was originally attached along the selvedge.\nOne sidehas been cut and hemmed."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/9aaa3d50-e32d-3150-a955-9397a566d331/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/9aaa3d50-e32d-3150-a955-9397a566d331/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.114-1926" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O53776> .

